title: Ed's empty view was skg-for-ai not understanding the server's answer "that node is already the root of a view you hold". Mended in the tool, with a test.
pid: 82f73e58-6e81-40d5-a5cc-e1d38a00dd12
body: |2-
  After the switch, the view's root is Jeff's fork, so the server
  answers 'view 7642d4d5' on the same connection as it answers a client
  following a link to any open root: it names the switched view of your
  'to Jeff' ('(switch-to-view ID)'), and Emacs would land in that buffer.
  skg-for-ai read only the 'content' field, found none, and said the
  graph may lack the ID. Now 'view' prints the files of the view it
  landed in, and says on standard error why and how to view the node by
  itself (switch the view back first). The server's behaviour I left
  alone: landing in the open view is right, since that view already
  shows the fork from its owner's perspective, which a fresh view of it
  would too. Not Drew's.
